      "title": "RBA board members who voted against rate hike warned of ‘materially sharper downturn’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/myefo-mid-year-budget-update-australia-treasurer-jim-chalmers",
      "description": "<p>Minutes released from latest Reserve Bank meeting as Jim Chalmers says Myefo ‘will cut enough, but not too much’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Reserve Bank board members who voted against this month’s official interest rate hike were worried about a “materially sharper downturn” in the economy, arguing the RBA should wait to see how higher borrowing costs would hit households.</p><p>Minutes from the two-day meeting revealed how three of the nine board members believed it was “prudent to leave more time” to see how the preceding four rate increases would flow through to the economy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/myefo-mid-year-budget-update-australia-treasurer-jim-chalmers\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T04:05:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "CFMEU pushed to get notorious Bandidos member hired on construction project, Big Build royal commission hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/cfmeu-bandidos-bikie-joel-leavitt-big-build-royal-commission-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Bikie Joel Leavitt, who has a criminal history including riot, affray and assaulting police, tells inquiry he can’t recall why union was pushing for him</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A bikie and former CFMEU member says he can’t recall why union representatives were pushing hard to have him hired on a construction project.</p><p>Bandidos member Joel Leavitt gave evidence to the royal commission into alleged corruption across Victoria’s construction sector on Tuesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/17/cfmeu-bandidos-bikie-joel-leavitt-big-build-royal-commission-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T03:51:23"
